<item><title>Malawi&apos;s ruling party blames fuel shortages on US-Iran conflict</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mw/malawi-s-ruling-party-blames-fuel-shortages-on-us-iran-7a87f0/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mw/malawi-s-ruling-party-blames-fuel-shortages-on-us-iran-7a87f0/</guid><category>Malawi</category><description>Jappie Mhango, vice-president of the Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) for the North, said the shortages stem from turmoil in the Middle East, not the party&apos;s own decisions.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:35:16 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mw.jpg" length="31502" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mw.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
